.TH HMAP_HASH 3 "15 Mar 2023" "CB" "Library Functions"

.SH NAME
hmap_hash \- Compute the hash value for a key

.SH SYNOPSIS
.IB #include <lib/hmap_internal.h>

.IB int32
.IB hmap_hash(const void* key, size_t len);

.SH DESCRIPTION
The \fBhmap_hash\fR function computes the hash value for a key. It takes a pointer to the key and the length of the key as arguments.

The function takes the following parameters:
.IB const void*
A pointer to the key.
.IB size_t
The length of the key.

The function returns an integer representing the hash value of the key. The hash value is computed using a simple hash function that combines addition, left shift, and XOR operations.

The \fBhmap_hash\fR function is intended to be used to compute the hash value of a key for use in a hash map.

.SH EXAMPLES
The following example demonstrates how to use the \fBhmap_hash\fR function to compute the hash value of a key:

.nf
#include <stdio.h>
#include <lib/hmap_internal.h>

int main() {
    const char* key = "example1";
    size_t len = 8;

    int32 hash_value = hmap_hash(key, len);

    printf("Hash value for key '%s': %d\n", key, hash_value);

    return 0;
}
.nef